From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: dwc: retry a link that doesn't come back on resume

A controller that went down in L2 retrains its link on every resume, and
dw_pcie_wait_for_link() gives it 900 ms. Nothing tries again after that, so
one link that fails to train stays down, and the PM core resumes the Root
Port and its children on it.

An endpoint that had a link when the system went to sleep should still be
there.
Take the slot through the same teardown and bring-up as a suspend and
resume, once, before giving up on it: PERST#, the PHY and the controller go
down, and on Qualcomm the deinit hook removes the slot supply too, unless it
is always on like VCC_WLAN_3R9. Nothing below the Root Port has been resumed
yet, so nothing is using the link, and an empty slot doesn't get here.

Without a delay the supply would only be off for about a millisecond, and
the minimum off time of the SSD isn't documented, so keep the slot off for
3 s. A resume whose link comes up on the first attempt doesn't change.

This doesn't help an endpoint that stopped answering. Its link can stay
down after the retry as well, and what the driver of the device does then
is up to it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++--
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.h  |  1 +
 2 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
index 30adfa657..4431bdff1 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
@@ -24,6 +24,12 @@
 #include "../../pci.h"
 #include "pcie-designware.h"
 
+/*
+ * Time a slot stays off when its link is retried on resume. The deinit hook
+ * may remove the slot supply, and the SSD's minimum off time isn't documented.
+ */
+#define DW_PCIE_RESUME_RETRY_OFF_MS	3000
+
 static struct pci_ops dw_pcie_ops;
 static struct pci_ops dw_pcie_ecam_ops;
 static struct pci_ops dw_child_pcie_ops;
@@ -1226,7 +1232,8 @@ int dw_pcie_suspend_noirq(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 	int ret = 0;
 	u32 val;
 
-	if (!dw_pcie_link_up(pci))
+	pci->link_up_at_suspend = dw_pcie_link_up(pci);
+	if (!pci->link_up_at_suspend)
 		goto stop_link;
 
 	if (!pci_host_common_d3cold_possible(pci->pp.bridge, &pme_capable))
@@ -1294,11 +1301,13 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(dw_pcie_suspend_noirq);
 
 int dw_pcie_resume_noirq(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 {
+	bool retry = pci->link_up_at_suspend;
 	int ret;
 
 	if (!pci->suspended)
 		return 0;
 
+bring_up:
 	if (pci->pp.ops->init) {
 		ret = pci->pp.ops->init(&pci->pp);
 		if (ret) {
@@ -1313,6 +1322,24 @@ int dw_pcie_resume_noirq(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_deinit;
 
+	ret = dw_pcie_wait_for_link(pci);
+
+	/*
+	 * The endpoint had a link before the suspend, so it should still be
+	 * there, and nothing below the Root Port has been resumed yet. Take the
+	 * slot down once more before giving up on it.
+	 */
+	if (ret && retry) {
+		dev_warn(pci->dev, "Link didn't come back (%d), taking the slot down\n",
+			 ret);
+		retry = false;
+		dw_pcie_stop_link(pci);
+		if (pci->pp.ops->deinit)
+			pci->pp.ops->deinit(&pci->pp);
+		msleep(DW_PCIE_RESUME_RETRY_OFF_MS);
+		goto bring_up;
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * The PM core resumes the Root Port and its children whatever happens
 	 * here, and they reach the controller through the DBI. Keep the host
@@ -1320,8 +1347,6 @@ int dw_pcie_resume_noirq(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 	 * link check in dw_pcie_other_conf_map_bus(), while tearing the host
 	 * down would leave the DBI unclocked.
 	 */
-	dw_pcie_wait_for_link(pci);
-
 	if (pci->pp.ops->post_init)
 		pci->pp.ops->post_init(&pci->pp);
 
diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.h b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.h
index 1d2139474..5674a6018 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.h
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.h
@@ -575,6 +575,7 @@ struct dw_pcie {
 	struct reset_control_bulk_data	core_rsts[DW_PCIE_NUM_CORE_RSTS];
 	struct gpio_desc		*pe_rst;
 	bool			suspended;
+	bool			link_up_at_suspend;
 	struct debugfs_info	*debugfs;
 	enum			dw_pcie_device_mode mode;
 	u16			ptm_vsec_offset;
